  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda &#x2013; Expansion coffee plantation &amp; processing facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF Start-up Loan Brand Development B.V. is able to further develop the existing coffee plantation Brand Coffee Farm Uganda.  The company acquired a plantation in 2017 and started planting coffee trees with their own resources and with support from a DGGF Technical Assistance subsidy. Coffee trees need at least five years to achieve a reasonable production, but already give fruit from year three. The farm is now in the first phase of development.The DGGF Start-up Loan is intended for the investment in buildings, machines and inventory for cultivation, as well as working capital to absorb the first start-up losses and for further expansion of the coffee plants.The expected impact is local employment of approximately 24 FTE and knowledge exchange to other coffee farmers (1.000 families) in the area in the field of production method, post harvesting handling and good agricultural practices.</narrative>
  </description>
